      "name": "Path dependency",
      "applied": "Ask where the switching cost actually is instead of asserting that the original choice was wrong.",
      "finding": "The switching cost sits with management's reform risk and operational change, not with technology: for students it is close to zero. And a caution: first come first served has partly persisted because it is genuinely simple and explicable, which is not the same as being locked in."
    }
  ],
  "tools_excluded": [
    {
      "name": "Multi-layer signal decoding (MLSD)",
      "excludedBecause": "The three admission questions fail: no sender with reputation at stake, no screening layer, no interest game between sender and receiver. Applied anyway, it would read management's silence as an encoded signal — finding signal in noise. Recorded rather than quietly dropped so the reader can see it was considered."
    }
